            aria-hidden="true"
            className="c9 c10"
            href="#summary"
            id="summary"
          >
            <img
              alt=""
              aria-hidden="true"
              height={12}
              src="test-file-stub"
              width={12}
            />
          </a>
          Summary
        </h2>
      </span>
      <p
        className="c11"
      >
        OurDNA data are available for download through
         
        <a
          className="c5"
          href="https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/requester-pays"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          a requester pays Google Cloud bucket
        </a>
        .
         
        <strong>
          Data access and download requires a Google Cloud account with billing enabled. Costs are billed to the user.
        </strong>
      </p>
      <p
        className="c11"
      >
        The data are maintained by the Centre for Population Genomics. We recommend using
         
        <a
          className="c5"
          href="https://hail.is/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          Hail
        </a>
         and
         
        <a
          className="c5"
          href="https://github.com/populationgenomics/gnomad_methods"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          the Centre for Population Genomics' fork of gnomad_methods
        </a>
         
        to work with OurDNA data. Please see our
         
        <a
          className="c12"
          href="/data-readme"
        >
          README
        </a>
         page for details on how OurDNA data differs from gnomAD data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Data can be browsed and downloaded from Google Cloud Storage using
         
        <a
          className="c5"
          href="https://cloud.google.com/sdk/gcloud/reference/storage"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          gcloud storage
        </a>
        .
      </p>
      <p>
        Replace 
        <b>
          YOUR_PROJECT_NAME
        </b>
         with your nominated Google project name for paying egress costs
      </p>
      <h4>
        Command to browse
      </h4>
       
      <p>
        <code
          className="c13"
        >
          gcloud storage ls --billing-project YOUR_PROJECT_NAME \\
          <br />
          gs://cpg-ourdna-browser-public-australia-southeast1/release
        </code>
      </p>
      <h4>
        Command to download (e.g. chr1 sites VCF)
      </h4>
       
      <p>
        <code
          className="c13"
        >
          gcloud storage cp --billing-project YOUR_PROJECT_NAME \\
          <br />
          gs://cpg-ourdna-browser-public-australia-southeast1/release/\\
          <br />
          1.0/vcf/exomes/chr1_variants.vcf.bgz .
        </code>
      </p>
